[2026-10-15T10:32:50.670Z] [INFO]         "content": "## Summary\n\n- Created `HelloWorld.scala` that prints \"Hello, World!\" exactly.\n- The program follows Scala best practices and includes comments explaining the code.\n- Build and run instructions are included as comments in the file.\n\n## Workflow Issue\n\nDue to permission restrictions on the token used by the AI agent, we were unable to create the GitHub Actions workflow file (`.github/workflows/test-hello-world.yml`). The agent encountered a 403 error when attempting to create or update workflow files.\n\n## Request\n\nWe request that either:\n1. The necessary permissions be granted to the agent to create workflow files, or\n2. A maintainer adds the workflow file separately.\n\nThe workflow should:\n- Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests\n- Set up Scala (using coursier/setup-scala@v1 with Scala 2.13.10)\n- Compile and run the HelloWorld.scala program\n- Verify the output is exactly \"Hello, World!\"\n\n## Testing\n\nThe Scala program has been tested locally (in an environment with Scala installed) and produces the expected output.\n\n---\n\n*This pull request resolves issue #3316*",
