[2026-10-15T10:33:18.533Z] [INFO]     "text": "I have implemented the Hello World program in Scala and created a pull request for the issue. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Changes Made\n1. **Created `HelloWorld.scala`** in the repository root:\n   - Prints exactly \"Hello, World!\" to the console\n   - Follows Scala best practices (object with main method, proper comments)\n   - Includes build/run instructions as comments in the file\n\n2. **Updated Pull Request #3317**:\n   - Updated the title to \"Implement Hello World in Scala\"\n   - Provided detailed description of the implementation\n   - Documented the workflow issue encountered\n   - Marked the PR as ready for review\n\n## Workflow Issue Encountered\nDue to permission restrictions on the token used by the AI agent, I was unable to create the required GitHub Actions workflow file (`.github/workflows/test-hello-world.yml`). The agent encountered a 403 error when attempting to create or update workflow files.\n\n## Request for Workflow Completion\nTo fully satisfy the issue requirements, either:\n1. Grant the necessary permissions to the agent to create workflow files, or\n2. A maintainer adds the workflow file separately\n\nThe workflow should:\n- Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests\n- Set up Scala (using coursier/setup-scala@v1 with Scala 2.13.10)\n- Compile and run `HelloWorld.scala`\n- Verify the output is exactly \"Hello, World!\"\n\nThe Scala program itself is complete and functional, producing the expected output when run in a Scala environment. The pull request is now ready for review and integration.",
