[2026-10-15T10:37:32.014Z] [INFO]     "text": "I have successfully implemented the Hello World program in Scala as requested in issue #3316. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n## ✅ Completed Tasks\n1. **Created `HelloWorld.scala`** with:\n   - Exact output: \"Hello, World!\"\n   - Proper Scala idioms (object with main method)\n   - Clear comments explaining the code\n   - Build/run instructions included as comments\n   - No external dependencies (standard library only)\n\n2. **Updated Pull Request #3317**:\n   - Title: \"Implement Hello World in Scala\"\n   - Detailed description of the implementation\n   - Documentation of the workflow permission issue encountered\n   - Marked as ready for review\n   - Base branch correctly set to `e2e/hello-world/38717502496/agent-nemotron-3-super-free` as requested\n\n## ⚠️ Workflow Limitation\nDue to permission restrictions on the token used by the AI agent, I was unable to create the required GitHub Actions workflow file (`.github/workflows/test-hello-world.yml`). The agent encountered a 403 error when attempting to create or update workflow files.\n\n## 📋 Request for Completion\nTo fully satisfy the issue requirements, either:\n1. Grant the necessary permissions to the agent to create workflow files, or  \n2. A maintainer adds the workflow file separately\n\nThe workflow should:\n- Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests\n- Set up Scala (using coursier/setup-scala@v1 with Scala 2.13.10)\n- Compile and run `HelloWorld.scala`\n- Verify the output is exactly \"Hello, World!\"\n\n## 🔍 Verification\nThe Scala program has been verified to produce the correct output:\n```\n$ scalac HelloWorld.scala\n$ scala HelloWorld\nHello, World!\n```\n\nThe pull request is now ready for review and integration. All code-related requirements have been met, and the only outstanding item is the GitHub Actions workflow, which is blocked by external permission constraints that have been clearly documented in the PR.",
